    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds pretty standard. i'm a bit worried about the transition between testing and staging though. sometimes things pass the automated tests but then everything just goes wrong right when we try to push it to the staging environment. how do we build better gates to stop those kinds of unexpected errors or \"hidden\" issues from slipping through?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address these environment-specific failures, implement infrastructure-as-code scanning during the testing phase to validate environment parity checks. You should also introduce service contract testing between microservices, ensuring APIs remain compatible regardless of where they are deployed. Furthermore, utilize contract testing to catch interface mismatches that automated unit tests often miss before they even reach staging. This proactive validation bridges the gap between local tests and the target environment.",
      "source": "target",
